body: `
<h2>Venn Diagram kya hai</h2><p>Venn diagram me har set ko ek vritt ya aakriti se dikhaya jata hai. Do vritton ka common hissa dono sets ke common elements ko dikhata hai, aur bahar ka hissa kisi bhi set me na hone wale elements ko dikhata hai. UPSC aur CSAT me isse survey, pasand, yogyata, aur syllogism jaise sawal poochhe jate hain. Sabse pehle yeh samajhna zaroori hai ki only A ka matlab hai A me hain par B me nahi, only B ka matlab hai B me hain par A me nahi, both ka matlab hai dono me hain, aur neither ka matlab hai kisi me bhi nahi.</p><h2>Do sets ke mukhya sutra</h2><p>Do sets A aur B ke liye n(A union B) = n(A) + n(B) - n(A intersection B) hota hai. Neither = Total - n(A union B). Only A = n(A) - n(A intersection B). Only B = n(B) - n(A intersection B). In sutron ko ratne ki jagah diagram banakar samajhna behtar hai. Diagram banate waqt hamesha andar se bahar ki taraf bharo, yani sabse pehle both ya common hissa likho, phir only wale hisse, aur ant me neither. Is kram se galti ki sambhavna bahut kam ho jati hai.</p><h2>Teen sets ka tareeka</h2><p>Teen sets me sabse andar wala hissa teeno ka common hota hai. Uske baad sirf do sets ke common hisse nikalte hain, phir sirf ek set ke hisse. Sutra hai n(A union B union C) = n(A) + n(B) + n(C) - n(A intersection B) - n(B intersection C) - n(C intersection A) + n(A intersection B intersection C). Yahan dhyan rakho ki do sets ke common diye gaye ankdon me teeno ka common bhi shamil hota hai, isliye only-do-sets wala hissa nikalne ke liye teeno wale hisse ko ghatana padta hai. Yahi ek chhoti si chook aksar galat uttar ka kaaran banti hai.</p><h2>Syllogism me Venn diagram</h2><p>Syllogism me kathanon ko diagram se jaancho. All A are B ka matlab hai A ka vritt poori tarah B ke andar hai. Some A are B ka matlab hai dono vritton me kuch common hissa hai. No A is B ka matlab hai dono vritt alag alag hain. Koi nishkarsh tabhi sahi mana jata hai jab woh har sambhav diagram me satya ho, sirf ek diagram me satya hona kaafi nahi hai. Isliye ek se zyada sambhav diagram banakar jaanchna ek achhi aadat hai. Kuch vishesh shabd jaise only, only a few, aur at least par vishesh dhyan do, kyunki ye diagram ki seema badal dete hain.</p><h2>Solved Example 1</h2><p>100 vidyarthiyon me 60 ko ganit pasand hai, 50 ko vigyan pasand hai, aur 30 ko dono pasand hain. Only ganit = 60 - 30 = 30. Only vigyan = 50 - 30 = 20. Dono me se koi ek pasand karne wale = 30 + 20 + 30 = 80. Kisi ko bhi pasand na karne wale = 100 - 80 = 20. Is sawal me andar se bahar ka kram hi poori kunji hai.</p><h2>Solved Example 2</h2><p>Ek sarvekshan me 200 logon me A = 90, B = 80, C = 70, A aur B = 35, B aur C = 25, A aur C = 20, aur teeno = 10 diye gaye. Only A aur B = 35 - 10 = 25. Only B aur C = 25 - 10 = 15. Only A aur C = 20 - 10 = 10. Only A = 90 - 25 - 10 - 10 = 45. Only B = 80 - 25 - 15 - 10 = 30. Only C = 70 - 10 - 15 - 10 = 35. Kam se kam ek pasand karne wale = 45 + 30 + 35 + 25 + 15 + 10 + 10 = 170. Koi bhi pasand na karne wale = 200 - 170 = 30.</p><h2>Exam tricks</h2><ul><li>Ankda likhne se pehle diagram banao, seedha jod-ghatav mat karo.</li><li>Percentage wale sawalon me total ko 100 maan lo, ganana aasan ho jayegi.</li><li>At least one ka matlab union hota hai, exactly one ka matlab only wale hisson ka yog hota hai.</li><li>Exactly two ka matlab sirf do sets wale hisson ka yog hota hai, teeno wala hissa isme nahi judta.</li><li>Neither poochha jaye to pehle union nikalo, phir total me se ghatayo.</li><li>Syllogism me possible diagram banane ke baad hi nishkarsh ko pakka mano.</li></ul><p>Ant me yaad rakho ki Venn diagram ek drishya upkaran hai. Diagram saaf banega to uttar bhi saaf milega, aur samay bhi bachega.</p>
`
