body: `
<h2>Alphabet series kya hai</h2><p>Alphabet series me aksharon ka ek kram diya jata hai aur agla akshar ya lupt akshar poochha jata hai. Har akshar ki ek sankhyatmak sthiti hoti hai: A = 1, B = 2, C = 3, aur isi tarah Z = 26. Series hal karne ka sabse pehla kadam har akshar ko uski sankhya me badalna hai, phir sankhyaon ke antar ko dekhna hai. Agar antar sthir hai to yeh samanya antar wali series hai, agar antar badh raha hai ya ghat raha hai to yeh badhta ya ghatta antar wali series hai.</p><h2>Mukhya pattern</h2><p>Pehla pattern sthir antar hai, jaise har baar 3 judna. Doosra pattern badhta antar hai, jaise 2, phir 3, phir 4, phir 5. Teesra pattern ulta kram hai, jaise har baar 2 ghatna. Chautha pattern jode wala hai, jaise A, Z, B, Y, C, X, jisme pehla akshar aage badhta hai aur doosra peechhe hat-ta hai. Paanchwa pattern wrap-around hai, jisme Z ke baad phir A aa jata hai. Udaaharan ke liye Z se 5 aage badhne par E milta hai, kyunki 26 + 5 = 31 aur 31 - 26 = 5. Chhatha pattern varg ya ghan jaisa antar ho sakta hai, jaise antar 1, 4, 9, 16 ho.</p><h2>Hal karne ka tareeka</h2><p>Sabse pehle sabhi aksharon ki sankhya likho. Phir aas-paas ke aksharon ka antar nikalo. Antar dekhkar pattern pehchano. Agar pattern turant na dikhe to aksharon ko ek chhodkar do bhagon me baant kar dekho, kyunki kai series me do alag series ek saath chalti hain. Udaaharan ke liye pehle, teesre, paanchwe akshar ek series banate hain aur doosre, chauthe, chhathe doosri. Agar akshar peechhe ki taraf ja rahe hain to ulta antar nikalo, aur agar Z paar ho raha hai to 26 ghatakar wrap-around lagao. Ant me mile akshar ko wapas sankhya se akshar me badalkar jaanch lo.</p><h2>Solved Example 1</h2><p>Series: A, C, F, J, O, ? Sankhyayen: 1, 3, 6, 10, 15. Antar: 2, 3, 4, 5. Agla antar 6 hoga. 15 + 6 = 21, yani U. Isliye agla akshar U hai. Yeh badhte antar ka classic udaaharan hai.</p><h2>Solved Example 2</h2><p>Series: A, Z, B, Y, C, X, ? Yahan jode bante hain: A ke saath Z, B ke saath Y, C ke saath X. Agla joda D ke saath W hoga. Series me saatwan sthan D ka hai, isliye uttar D hai. Agar aathwan poochha jata to uttar W hota.</p><h2>Solved Example 3</h2><p>Series: Q, S, V, Z, ? Sankhyayen: 17, 19, 22, 26. Antar: 2, 3, 4. Agla antar 5 hoga. 26 + 5 = 31, 31 - 26 = 5, yani E. Isliye uttar E hai. Yahan wrap-around ki jaanch zaroori thi, warna galat uttar milta.</p><h2>Exam tricks</h2><ul><li>Har akshar ki sankhya likhna kabhi mat chhodo, andaze se kaam mat lo.</li><li>Antar na mile to ek chhodkar wali do series aazmao.</li><li>Z ke baad A wala wrap-around hamesha dhyan me rakho.</li><li>Vyanjan aur swar ka kram bhi kabhi pattern ho sakta hai, is par bhi nazar rakho.</li><li>Do aksharon wali series me pehle aur doosre akshar ke pattern alag alag ho sakte hain.</li><li>Uttar milne ke baad poori series ko ek baar phir se jaanch lo.</li></ul><p>Alphabet series me gati hi sab kuch hai. Sankhya me badalna, antar nikalna, aur pattern lagana, bas in teen kadmon ka abhyas hi aapko tez banayega.</p>
`
